# Job Search Project: shared rules (example)

This file loads in every session. Agent specs add role-specific rules; skills add step-by-step methods.

## Candidate (fictional)

Alex Rivera. Target: Growth and GTM strategy roles in US tech.

## Load in order

@./rules/01_identity_and_positioning.md
@./rules/02_target_roles.md
@./rules/03_truth_rules.md
@./rules/04_workflows.md
@./rules/05_tone.md
@./rules/06_file_map.md

## Hard rules

1. Facts come only from `sources/master_cv.docx`, `sources/master_profile.md` and `sources/story_bank.md`. If a fact is missing, ask. Never write it.
2. Score fit against the job post's literal text. Say clearly when a role is a weak fit.
3. CVs are one page.
4. Agents draft. The candidate approves and sends.
5. Return the full path of the file you wrote. Do not create copies elsewhere.

## Change history

Each rule change gets a dated line here with the reason.
